[
  {
    "sha": "e7d7b1b2da10370b46b982bb280bc40a7176ae7b",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVVonwNoAKGU3ZDdiMWIyZGExMDM3MGI0NmI5ODJiYjI4MGJjNDBhNzE3NmFlN2I",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-23T06:47:45Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-23T06:47:45Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(multiaxis): Rotary Parallel cuts the full turn of the bar\n\nThe laid swarf raster finished the bar from above only: the bottom\nquadrant counted as shallow ground that the raster never reaches, the\nrings skipped it, and the ladder stopped at Bottom read as a tip height.\nOn a laid bar 126 degrees stayed uncut; on the example about a quarter.\n\nThe rotary path now plans the bar in two halves: the laid frame and the\nsame frame turned half a turn about the axis. Each half keeps the cut\nover its own upper half, the turned half is carried back by the rigid\nhalf turn, and the seam keeps each pass once. The turned half is held\nto Bottom where the radial ball touches the bar, so a Bottom above the\naxis still keeps the cut to the upper arc. The raster and ring notes now\nreach the path, and a full-turn path says it needs a full turn of A.\n\nbuild_sups and every shared finishing helper are unchanged. The example\nprogram and project are regenerated with WRITE_GOLDEN=1; the guide page,\nits pictures and its pins follow.\n\nFixes #2970\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
