  {
    "sha": "bfefff3bd65cfdf930e87a46d69a017421b22e67",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVVonwNoAKGJmZWZmZjNiZDY1Y2ZkZjkzMGU4N2E0NmQ2OWEwMTc0MjFiMjJlNjc",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-23T07:33:09Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-23T07:33:09Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(multiaxis): Rotary Parallel halves lose no single-frame cut\n\nReview of PR #3650: on a part that is not round the plane seam dropped\ncuts the single laid frame made - a keyway's lower wall, cut by half A\nwith its ball centre under the seam and out of half B's sight. A cut of\nA under the seam now stays unless B cuts the same place (within half a\npass spacing); a cut of B over the seam is added where A cuts nothing\nnear (a wall that faces down). A reach reading on a fixed station x\nangle grid names the arcs no pass reaches; only a path with none says\nit goes all the way round. Round bars keep their output.\n\nThe test reference is the generator as it stood before the halves\n(single_frame_tests.rs, test only): the keyed bar lost 52 centre samples\nbefore this change and loses none now, and no place is cut twice. The\noperations test bound reads each half's own law and the touch in world\nz for every feed and plunge; a keyed bar in bar stock verifies clean.\n\nRefs #2970\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
