      },
      "message": "test(app): Rotary Parallel bounds that can fail, and the corner verdict\n\nThe per-half Bottom reads in operations.rs could not fail on that bar;\nthey are gone, and the world-z touch bound on every feed and plunge,\nthe counts of both halves and the sector check are the bounds (a Bottom\n1 mm higher in the bound makes it red). The keyed bar accepts only the\nenvelope verdict at the keyway with its gouge within 0.05 mm. The\ndecision file states that the round outputs stayed the same on the run\nfixtures, not by a law, and names the follow-up #3658.\n\nRefs #2970\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
